WEBVTT

00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:14,360
Is there a good protein product to use for the goal?

00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:22,440
So yeah, I recommend the U.S. enzyme protein mixes

00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:25,640
because they're low in glutamine.

00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:31,080
There are some protein mixes that have higher glutamine.

00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:35,840
I also trust U.S. enzymes because I think of all

00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:45,160
the supplement companies out there, U.S. enzymes, and PRL are probably the two clearest

00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:53,800
beating that they're the most anal companies as far as protecting their clients with

00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,440
purity.

00:00:55,440 --> 00:01:01,600
So most supplements, you know, the supplement companies have to buy their raw product from

00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:04,480
some place.

00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:10,600
And whether you like it or not, a lot of raw product is purchased from China.

00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:17,660
All the green tea extract, all the EGCG extract in every supplement is there's not made

00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:20,400
anywhere but China.

00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:29,280
And you know, these producers in China will basically be, you know, discriminate to who

00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:32,200
they send their clearest stuff to.

00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:41,400
So if they send a giant barrel, it comes actually in these giant bags on a pallet.

00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:47,440
They send a pallet of green tea extract EGCG to U.S. enzymes or PRL.

00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:51,840
They test the batch, not just the top of the batch, but they test all the way through the

00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,840
batch.

00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:57,360
And if it doesn't, if it tests contaminated at all, it gets sent back and the way they have

00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:01,840
the contract with the company is that they don't have to pay for the shipping in an excise

00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:05,560
and everything so they don't ever want to get a batch back.

00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:09,840
So clean products are important to me.

00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:17,520
I know other companies, you know, do testing as well and that we only sell, we only recommend

00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:20,680
companies that we feel like are the clearest.

00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:26,800
And that's a difference between if you bought your supplements at Walmart or Walgreens or Target

00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,640
or something like that.

00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:34,480
So you want clean supplements, but then when you're looking at a protein powder for a cancer

00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:39,440
patient, you want a protein powder that has the least amount of glutamated in it.

00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:45,040
And we've settled out the U.S. enzymes product for that for protein.

00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:48,600
They have a chocolate and they have a vanilla, it's very good.

00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:52,720
We use it a lot and a lot of people like it.

00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:57,360
But you know what I've said about protein powders in the past, that's why this person asked

00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:02,800
this question for how to go, is that you're only still getting 20 to 25 grams of protein

00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:09,120
in a protein powder drink, which is far less than you get from a piece of chicken.

00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:18,080
So it's really hard to get your protein levels up by just assuming a protein powder.

00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:22,360
But I understand if you're on the go, you want to add a little bit of protein to a shake

00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:25,480
or something, there's nothing wrong with adding a protein powder, you get that little bit

00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:31,400
of boost, I would use the protein powder from U.S. enzymes.

